                <pb facs="0962" n="872" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg872"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">815.51/383a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul in Chargé of the
                        Legation in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lawton</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-12-15T10:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 15,
                                1919—10 a.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Department desires that if possible during an informal conversation with
                    President Bográn you discreetly discuss with him the desirability of having a
                    report prepared of the Honduran financial system with a view to eventually
                    placing Honduran finances on a satisfactory basis. It is suggested that if
                    possible Bográn request the Department for the services of an expert to make the
                    report referred to.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
